{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960904-funny-open-call-the-vaporwave-chroncicle","id":960904,"title":"[Funny, Open Call] - The Vaporwave Chroncicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T23:17:43-07:00","id":960904,"title":"[Funny, Open Call] - The Vaporwave Chroncicle","content":"The butt of countless internet jokes and favored genre/aesthetic of insufferable pretentious folks (like your truly), vaporwave is as divisive as it is inexplicable. Sometimes likened to &quot;elevator music from hell,&quot; vaporwave is a dissonant combination of ambient music and surreal visuals that act as a kind of late 80s to early 90s, abandoned shopping mall/office space, Web 1.0 nightmare, full of low-quality 3D polygons, marble statues, and potted plants, all to the tune of <a href=\"https://beerontherug.bandcamp.com/track/420\" target=\"_blank\">remixed-beyond-all-recognition dated pop music </a>and <a href=\"https://disconscious.bandcamp.com/track/lunar-food-court-4\" target=\"_blank\">food court noises.</a> Some take it as a postmodern satire of the corporate capitalist optimism of decades past, when a booming economy and new technology promised a future that would never be; others like to point and laugh at the absurdity of a Roman bust floating on a Windows 95 desktop as a political statement.<br /> <br /> But the Chronicles of Darkness is nothing if not a versatile toolkit, and what's the point of trying to be modular and adaptable if you can't simulate the unique horror provided by sinister virtual dreams and the ruins of the early Internet? So I ask you, dear forum posters: how do we make the CofD more... <i>a e s t h e t i c ?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakk